    "title": "LESSON 7: THE IMPERATIF",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "L'IMPÉRATIF gives commands — just",
          "drop the subject pronoun from the",
          "present tense. Three forms: tu,",
          "nous, vous.",
          "",
          "-ER verbs DROP the final -s on tu:   Press 1",
          "tu parles  → Parle !  (Speak!)",
          "nous parlons → Parlons !  (Let's speak!)",
          "vous parlez → Parlez !  (Speak!)",
          "",
          "-IR/-RE verbs KEEP the -s:            Press 2",
          "tu finis → Finis !  (Finish!)",
          "tu vends → Vends !  (Sell!)"
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Leçon sept",
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "parle, parlons, parlez",
          "2": "finis, vends"
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "FOUR IRREGULAR IMPERATIVES to",
          "memorize — they don't just drop",
          "the pronoun:",
          "",
          "ÊTRE:                                Press 1",
          "sois, soyons, soyez",
          "",
          "AVOIR:                               Press 2",
          "aie, ayons, ayez",
          "",
          "SAVOIR:                              Press 3",
          "sache, sachons, sachez",
          "",
          "ALLER:                               Press 4",
          "va, allons, allez",
          "",
          "Ferme la porte ! (Close the door!)",
          "Écoute ! (Listen!)"
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "sois, soyons, soyez",
          "2": "aie, ayons, ayez",
          "3": "sache, sachons, sachez",
          "4": "va, allons, allez"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
